WEBVTT

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:20.790
GRAVES: You're upset.

00:00:22.583 --> 00:00:23.918
It's your mother again.

00:00:25.211 --> 00:00:26.587
Somebody said something.

00:00:27.171 --> 00:00:28.589
What did they say? Tell me.

00:00:29.298 --> 00:00:30.466
Do you think I'm a freak?

00:00:30.633 --> 00:00:33.594
No. I think you're
a very special young man,

00:00:33.761 --> 00:00:36.889
or I wouldn't have
asked you to help me, now would I?

00:00:41.477 --> 00:00:42.853
Have you any news?

00:00:44.272 --> 00:00:45.314
I'm still looking.

00:00:45.481 --> 00:00:46.482
Mmm.

00:00:49.569 --> 00:00:51.821
Mr. Graves, if I knew
whether it was a girl or a boy--

00:00:51.988 --> 00:00:55.366
My vision showed
only the child's immense power.

00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:58.369
He or she is no older than 10.

00:00:59.954 --> 00:01:02.582
I saw this child
in close proximity to your mother.

00:01:02.748 --> 00:01:05.084
She I saw so plainly.

00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:07.044
That could be any one of hundreds--

00:01:07.211 --> 00:01:09.964
There's something else.
Something I haven't told you.

00:01:10.131 --> 00:01:12.466
I saw you beside me in New York.

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:17.013
You're the one who gains
this child's trust.

00:01:17.179 --> 00:01:19.974
You are the key. I saw this.

00:01:20.141 --> 00:01:23.144
You want to join the wizarding world.

00:01:23.811 --> 00:01:26.063
I want those things too, Credence.

00:01:26.230 --> 00:01:27.648
I want them for you.

00:01:29.025 --> 00:01:30.776
So find the child.

00:01:31.694 --> 00:01:33.654
Find the child and we'll all be free.

00:01:36.324 --> 00:01:37.908
QUEENIE: The job ain't that glamorous.

00:01:38.075 --> 00:01:40.161
I mean, I spend most days making coffee.

00:01:40.328 --> 00:01:41.871
Unjinxing the john.

00:01:42.079 --> 00:01:43.623
Tina's the career girl.

00:01:43.956 --> 00:01:45.124
(1920s MUSIC PLAYING ON RADIO)

00:01:46.292 --> 00:01:47.501
Nah, we're orphans.

00:01:47.918 --> 00:01:51.005
Ma and Pa died of Dragon Pox
when we were kids.

00:01:52.632 --> 00:01:53.633
Oh.

00:01:54.008 --> 00:01:55.009
You're sweet.

00:01:55.926 --> 00:01:57.428
But we got each other.

00:01:59.472 --> 00:02:01.849
Could you stop
reading my mind for a second?

00:02:02.099 --> 00:02:03.100
Oh...

00:02:03.392 --> 00:02:05.853
Don't get me wrong, I love it.

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:07.271
(BOTH LAUGH)

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:10.149
This meal, it's insanely good.

00:02:10.858 --> 00:02:12.234
And this is what I do, I'm a cook.

00:02:12.401 --> 00:02:16.530
And this is like the greatest meal
I have ever had in my life.

00:02:16.697 --> 00:02:17.948
(BOTH LAUGHING)

00:02:19.909 --> 00:02:21.744
Oh! You slay me.

00:02:22.203 --> 00:02:24.872
I ain't never
really talked to a No-Maj before.

00:02:25.039 --> 00:02:26.374
Huh.

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:27.833
Really?

00:02:34.715 --> 00:02:36.384
I am not flirting.

00:02:41.472 --> 00:02:43.182
I'm just saying,
don't go getting attached.

00:02:43.432 --> 00:02:45.267
He's gonna have to be Obliviated.

00:02:46.727 --> 00:02:47.937
It's nothing personal.

00:02:48.729 --> 00:02:50.648
Oh, hey, you okay, honey?

00:02:50.815 --> 00:02:54.443
So, Ms. Goldstein, I think Mr. Kowalski
could do with an early night.

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:55.611
Besides, you and I will need to be

00:02:55.778 --> 00:02:58.155
up early tomorrow morning
to find my Niffler, so...

00:02:59.699 --> 00:03:00.741
What's a Niffler?

00:03:01.951 --> 00:03:03.285
Don't ask.

00:03:04.203 --> 00:03:05.913
Hey, you guys can bunk in here.

00:03:15.214 --> 00:03:16.215
(KNOCK ON DOOR)

00:03:22.430 --> 00:03:24.932
Uh, I thought you might like a hot drink.

00:03:35.234 --> 00:03:36.277
JACOB: (SIGHS) Wow!

00:03:37.111 --> 00:03:41.115
Psst! Hey. Mr. Scamander, look, cocoa.

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:45.119
Toilet's down the hall to the right.

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:47.288
Thanks.

00:03:50.833 --> 00:03:52.251
Very much.

00:03:52.418 --> 00:03:53.419
(DOOR CLOSES)

00:03:53.586 --> 00:03:54.587
(WHISTLES)

00:04:04.513 --> 00:04:05.514
(HIGH-PITCHED GASP)

00:04:07.349 --> 00:04:08.350
(FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING)

00:04:11.145 --> 00:04:12.146
(FOOTSTEPS RECEDING)

00:04:15.524 --> 00:04:16.942
NEWT: Come on.

00:04:18.194 --> 00:04:19.487
(FOOTSTEPS RECEDING)

00:04:32.792 --> 00:04:34.251
For the love--

00:04:44.178 --> 00:04:46.096
-(OBJECTS CLATTERING)
-(GRUNTS)

00:04:46.263 --> 00:04:47.973
(BOTH BUZZING)

00:04:49.016 --> 00:04:50.100
NEWT: Will you sit down?

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:53.229
Good idea.

00:04:57.942 --> 00:04:59.151
That's definitely the Murtlap.

00:04:59.318 --> 00:05:01.278
You must be particularly susceptible.

00:05:02.154 --> 00:05:03.614
See, you're a Muggle,

00:05:04.281 --> 00:05:06.116
so our physiologies are subtly different.

00:05:13.165 --> 00:05:14.166
Ew!

00:05:14.875 --> 00:05:17.211
-Stay still.
-Ah...

00:05:17.545 --> 00:05:18.879
That should stop the sweating.

00:05:19.046 --> 00:05:20.840
And one of those should sort the twitch.

00:05:28.097 --> 00:05:29.431
-Here, take that.
-Ugh...

00:05:35.563 --> 00:05:36.897
Come on.

00:05:38.065 --> 00:05:39.275
Whatcha got there?

00:05:39.441 --> 00:05:43.070
This, the locals call Swooping Evil.

00:05:43.863 --> 00:05:45.573
Not the friendliest of names.

00:05:45.906 --> 00:05:47.783
It's quite an agile fella.

00:05:51.829 --> 00:05:53.914
I've been studying him,
and I'm pretty sure

00:05:54.081 --> 00:05:56.625
that his venom
could be quite useful if properly diluted.

00:05:56.917 --> 00:05:59.128
Just to remove bad memories, you know?

00:06:00.713 --> 00:06:01.714
(SCREECHING)

00:06:06.927 --> 00:06:09.305
Probably shouldn't let him
loose in here, though.

00:06:10.014 --> 00:06:11.056
(DOOR OPENS)

00:06:11.265 --> 00:06:12.474
Come on.

00:06:19.899 --> 00:06:21.191
(WIND HOWLING)

00:06:26.155 --> 00:06:27.197
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

00:06:27.656 --> 00:06:30.451
NEWT: Come on. Down you come.

00:06:30.618 --> 00:06:31.994
(SCREECHING)

00:06:36.165 --> 00:06:37.291
Come on.

